  Easy names at home

  When names don't work
  The names need internet name lookup. Some routers hide them, and a phone using its own name
  lookup may behave differently. Use the addresses with numbers when a name fails.

  If your network address changes
  The names contain this computer's network address. If your router changes it, old bookmarks stop
  working. Review the LAN address in Settings. Ask your router to keep the same address to avoid
  this.

  The internet
  self-host opens no port on your router. Do not forward port 80 to this computer; these pages are
  meant for your home network.

  Changing it later
  Everything here can be changed later in Settings, under Access.

  Technical details
  One managed Caddy in the Compose Project owns port 80 and routes HTTP requests by Host to each
  App. Names are <app>.<lan-ip-with-dashes>.sslip.io on every OS. sslip.io sees the LAN address in
  DNS queries. DNS-rebind protection can block names; the IP:port Address stays. Port conflicts
  and rootless Docker are refused without changes. HTTP is not encrypted; Apps that require HTTPS
  still require it. A DHCP reservation keeps bookmarks stable.

